4. Stochastic Viability, Epistemic Uncertainty, and Robust Resilience

4.1 Stochastic Extension with Manifold‑Preserving Noise

Adding random disturbances, we model the networked system as an Itô SDE

d\mathbf{x} = \bigl[ \mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x}) + \mathbf{G}(\mathbf{x}) \mathbf{u} \bigr] dt + \boldsymbol{\Sigma}(\mathbf{x}) d\mathbf{W}(t),

with the structural condition A \boldsymbol{\Sigma}_\ell(\mathbf{x}) = 0 for each compartment, so noise remains tangential to the mass‑conservation manifold. The stochastic viability kernel can be approximated via dynamic programming or learned via reinforcement learning with safety constraints.

Resilience is quantified by the expected minimal time of crisis (Doyen & Saint‑Pierre, 1997; Rougé et al., 2017):

R(\mathbf{x}) = \sup_{\mathbf{u}(\cdot)} \mathbb{E}[\tau_K(\mathbf{x})],

where \tau_K is the first exit time from K. This function unifies deterministic viability and stochastic survival analysis.

4.2 Robustness to Epistemic Uncertainty

The most dangerous threat to a closed biosphere is not white noise but structural model error — metabolic drift, unmodeled microbial interactions, or parameter shifts. We therefore introduce an explicit bounded perturbation term \boldsymbol{\Delta}(\mathbf{x}, t) with known bound \|\boldsymbol{\Delta}\|_\infty \le \delta. The dynamics become

\dot{\mathbf{x}} = \mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x}) + \mathbf{G}(\mathbf{x}) \mathbf{u} + \boldsymbol{\Delta}(\mathbf{x}, t), \qquad \|\boldsymbol{\Delta}\| \le \delta .

A Robust Control Barrier Function (RCBF) condition guarantees safety under all admissible perturbations:

\sup_{\mathbf{u}} \min_{(\ell,k) \in I(\mathbf{x})} \left[ \langle \nabla g_k^{(\ell)}, f_\ell + G_\ell u^{(\ell)} + \text{transport} \rangle - \delta \|\nabla g_k^{(\ell)}\| \right] \ge -\alpha(h).
\tag{3}

When the uncertainty bound \delta is conservatively estimated, this provides a safety margin. For long‑duration missions, we can additionally employ Adaptive CBFs that update the model parameters online when the digital twin detects discrepancy, thereby tightening the bound \delta and reducing conservatism over time.

