Appendix G. Constrained Kalman Filter for Mass‑Conservation Manifold

G.1 System Model

The true state \mathbf{x}_k \in \mathbb{R}^{nN} evolves in discrete time (after numerical discretization) but is subject to the linear equality constraint

A_{\text{glob}} \mathbf{x}_k = M_{\text{total}}, \quad \mathbf{x}_k \ge 0.

Measurements are y_k = H_k \mathbf{x}_k + v_k with v_k \sim \mathcal{N}(0,R_k). The unconstrained Kalman filter (prediction and update) yields an estimate \hat{\mathbf{x}}_{k|k} that generally does not satisfy the constraint.

G.2 Projection Step

To restore the constraint, we solve the constrained weighted least‑squares problem:

\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{k|k}^{\text{con}} = \arg\min_{\mathbf{x}} (\mathbf{x} - \hat{\mathbf{x}}_{k|k})^\top P_{k|k}^{-1} (\mathbf{x} - \hat{\mathbf{x}}_{k|k}) \quad \text{s.t.} \quad A_{\text{glob}} \mathbf{x} = M_{\text{total}},\; \mathbf{x} \ge 0.

The equality constraint alone yields a closed‑form solution (see Simon & Chia, 2002):

\hat{\mathbf{x}}^{\text{eq}} = \hat{\mathbf{x}}_{k|k} - P_{k|k} A_{\text{glob}}^\top (A_{\text{glob}} P_{k|k} A_{\text{glob}}^\top)^{-1} (A_{\text{glob}} \hat{\mathbf{x}}_{k|k} - M_{\text{total}}).

If the resulting estimate violates non‑negativity, we solve the quadratic program with inequality constraints, which is a small‑scale QP efficiently handled by active‑set methods. The projected estimate remains a minimum‑variance unbiased estimate under the constraints and can be fed into the next prediction step, maintaining consistency.

G.3 Covariance Update

The covariance matrix after projection can be updated via the linear projection operator \Pi = I - P_{k|k} A_{\text{glob}}^\top (A_{\text{glob}} P_{k|k} A_{\text{glob}}^\top)^{-1} A_{\text{glob}} as

P_{k|k}^{\text{con}} = \Pi P_{k|k} \Pi^\top,

which reflects the reduced uncertainty along the constraint surface. This constrained Kalman filter guarantees that the digital twin never violates atomic conservation.

